>> title: Teriyaki Chicken Bowl
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: chicken, rice, kale, japanese, skillet, bowl
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: teriyaki bowl, chicken teriyaki bowl, teriyaki rice bowl, teriyaki chicken, sesame kale bowl, rice bowl, grain bowl, power bowl
>> pairs-with: teriyaki-sauce, shichimi-togarashi
>> servings: 4
>> time: 45 min
>> slack: narrow — the glaze is mostly sugar, and a minute past sticky it turns bitter; there is no rinsing it back off the chicken

>> step: The glaze goes on at the very end and over low heat. In a hot pan early it is bitter before the chicken is cooked.
The glaze goes on at the very end and over low heat.

>> step: steam 18 min, rest 10 min, lid on
Steam @short-grain rice{1 1/2%cups}(300 g; rinsed until the water runs clear) with @water{1 3/4%cups}(415 mL) in a covered #saucepan{} ~steam{18%min}, then ~rest{10%min} off the heat with the lid still on.

>> step: sear 9 min, both faces brown
Sear @chicken thighs{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; boneless, skinless) in @vegetable oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) in a #skillet{} ~sear{9%min}, turning once, until both faces are properly brown and the thickest part is firm.

>> step: glaze over low heat 2 min
Turn @&(~1)chicken{} through @teriyaki sauce{1/2%cup}(120 mL) over low heat ~toss{2%min}, until the sauce tightens into a coat that clings, then lift it out and slice across the grain.

>> step: wilt 4 min, dress off the heat
Wilt @kale{6%cups}(packed; stems stripped, torn) with @garlic{2%cloves}(sliced) in @toasted sesame oil{2%tsp}(10 mL) in a #skillet{} ~saute{4%min}, then off the heat toss it through @toasted sesame seeds{1%Tbs} and @rice vinegar{2%tsp}.

>> step: build it, kale beside the chicken
Spoon @&(~4)rice{} into four bowls, lay @&(~2)glazed chicken{} and @&(~1)sesame kale{} across it, and scatter over @cucumber{1/2}(sliced thin), @scallions{2}(sliced on the bias) and @shichimi togarashi{1/2%tsp}.
